.TH S3M-FIND 1 "" "s3m @VERSION@" "s3m Manual"
.SH NAME
s3m\-find \- parallel find for object storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3m\-find
[\fIS3M\-OPTIONS\fR] \fBs3://\fIBUCKET\fR[\fB/\fIPREFIX\fR]... [\fIEXPRESSION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Searches buckets in parallel, evaluating a
.BR find (1)-style
expression against every object.
s3m options come first, then URIs, then the expression.
With no expression everything matches.
Every test is answered from the listing, so no per-object requests are made.
.PP
There is deliberately no \fB\-delete\fR and no \fB\-exec\fR: s3m\-find only reads.
Pipe matches to
.BR xargs (1)
(via \fB\-print0\fR) or to
.BR s3m\-rm (1),
which has its own dry run.
.SH S3M OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " N"
Worker threads, 1\-256 (default 16).
.TP
.BI \-\-shard\-depth " N"
Prefix levels expanded for parallelism, 0\-9 (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-versions
Search every stored version and delete marker.
Output gains a \fBversion_id\fR column and \fB\-latest\fR and \fB\-marker\fR become available.
.TP
.B \-\-rrdns
Resolve the endpoint hostname to every A/AAAA address and spread worker threads across them, moving a thread to the next address if its current one fails.
See
.BR s3m (7).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write matches to FILE and show live progress.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
No listing; the summary still shows the match count.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH TESTS
.TP
.BR \-name " G, " \-iname " G"
Glob on the last path segment of the key.
.TP
.BR \-key " G, " \-ikey " G"
Glob on the whole key (\fB*\fR also spans \fB/\fR).
.TP
.BR \-regex " R, " \-iregex " R"
POSIX extended regex, anchored to the whole key.
.TP
.BR \-size " [+\-]N[ckMGT]"
Size, rounded up to the unit (default \fBc\fR, bytes).
.TP
.BR \-mtime " [+\-]N"
Age in days, with find's rounding rules.
.TP
.BR \-mmin " [+\-]N"
Age in minutes.
.TP
.BR \-class " C"
Storage class (case-insensitive).
.TP
.BR \-etag " E"
Exact etag (quotes optional).
.TP
.B \-empty
Zero-byte object.
.TP
.BR \-latest ", " \-marker
Current version / delete marker (with \fB\-\-versions\fR).
.TP
.BR \-true ", " \-false
Constants.
.SH OPERATORS
In order of precedence, highest first, as in find:
.PP
.RS
.nf
( EXPR )   ! EXPR, \-not EXPR   EXPR EXPR, EXPR \-a EXPR   EXPR \-o EXPR
.fi
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
CSV with a \fBkey\fR header (\fBkey,version_id\fR with \fB\-\-versions\fR).
With \fB\-print0\fR, NUL-separated raw keys for \fBxargs \-0\fR.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
The connection options \fB\-\-endpoint\fR, \fB\-\-region\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-\-path\-style\fR, \fB\-\-no\-sign\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR and \fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR are common to all s3m tools and are described in
.BR s3m (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 completed with errors; 2 usage, startup or safety-guard refusal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3m (7)
.BR s3m\-ls (1),
.BR s3m\-rm (1)
